  "goodToKnow": "Der Chirurg (die Chirurgin) is a surgeon; die Chirurgie is surgery as a field or hospital department, and chirurgisch means surgical. Careful: a British doctor's surgery is die Praxis, and an operation is die Operation (OP). The ch is pronounced as in ich in the north (çi-RURK) and as k in the south. It's a weak noun: den Chirurgen. Plural: die Chirurgen."
